The debug signing configuration was empty and relied on implicit behavior from the Android Gradle Plugin (AGP). This PR addresses the issue by adding an explicit debug build type with clear documentation explaining the intentional use of AGP defaults.

**Changes Made:**
- Added explicit `debug` build type in `CleverFerret/build.gradle.kts`
- Added comments explaining that the empty block intentionally uses AGP defaults including the default debug keystore
- No functional changes to the actual signing behavior - debug builds continue to work exactly as before

**Before:**
```kotlin
buildTypes {
    release {
        // ... release configuration
    }
    // Debug build type was implicit
}
```

**After:**
```kotlin
buildTypes {
    debug {
        // Intentionally empty - uses AGP defaults including the default debug keystore
        // This provides automatic debug signing without requiring explicit configuration
    }
    release {
        // ... release configuration
    }
}
```

This follows Android development best practices by using AGP defaults for debug builds while making the intent explicit through documentation. Debug builds automatically use the Android debug keystore without requiring manual configuration, which is the standard approach for development builds.

Fixes #45.

